---
description: Push opentoolbook8 to main. Do not ask for a review.
alwaysApply: true
---

You own this repository. Commit on `main` and push to `origin main`.

Do not open a pull request, do not create a branch, and do not ask the user to check or merge your work.

Run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` and get a pass before the push. One settled behavior per push. Anything not in `SETTLED.md` is not implemented.

Write notes into the repo in the same push that produces them. Product and engine notes go in `RESEARCH.md`, with the source named.

OpenScript is the language. Book script is the source text in a `.sbk` or a `.tbk`. Core is the DLLs and EXEs. `python3 -m opentoolbook book.tbk` prints a report. It does not open a window and it does not run `enterapplication`, `entersystem`, `gotopagelist`, or `opensession`. `--show PAGE` draws that page id. It does not follow those handlers to the book's opening page.

The ToolBook 8.1 authoring installer is the one Denny Dedmore's reinstall page lists (`DENNY-RUNTIME.md`). Never record a serial number. Never commit a proprietary binary or DLL. Do not force-disassemble unknown data. No `ForceDisassembleC8` and no `ForceDisassemblePrologues`. Describe code that a call path or a clean import reached. Do not run Ghidra.

opentoolbook8 is a ToolBook 8 reader. It opens a book, draws the page, and runs the book's OpenScript. Foolbook is the other viewer. Do not import Foolbook, do not copy its painter, and do not treat Foolbook as right where it disagrees with ToolBook. ToolBook 8 is the target. A painted value comes from a reader. A reader comes from bytes that repeat across the lesson, not from one example and not from a guess that makes the picture look finished. Each push makes the window or the engine do something a person can see. Tests pass before the push. SETTLED.md lists every new fact that push implements. FINDINGS.md is only for a byte the viewer is blocked on. A push that only adds a note is a failed push.
